          "quote": "The seat of the arbitration shall be in Osaka, Japan, if it is demanded by Array, and in New York, NY, USA, if it is demanded by Ono, with hearings to held in the same location.",
          "rationale": "Section 18.3 selects the laws of the State of New York (without conflict-of-law reference and excluding the CISG), which is the playbook's preferred governing law. Disputes are resolved by ICC arbitration under Section 17.3 rather than in New York courts, but the seat mechanic is not adverse to us: as the Japanese party (Ono), we arbitrate at home in Osaka whenever Array commences proceedings, and in New York — an accepted venue — when we commence. There is therefore no exclusive foreign seat in the counterparty's home jurisdiction and no walk-away trigger; Section 17.3(g) also preserves each Party's right to apply to any court of competent jurisdiction for provisional and conservatory relief. The substitution of arbitration for the preferred court venue is a sub-element short of the preferred wording that operates in our favour, so we note it rather than redline it.",
